IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch17-19`

-- Tests for chapters 17 to 19.  Every expected value was written from the text before the
-- file was run; unit ids (17.1, 18.2 ...) are those of the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- Exception: the assertions marked `-- RECONCILED` were re-derived after a first run, each from the text and the rule, and each comment quotes the original:
-- in the first pass those that expected a no where the text does not say no in its own words, and in the second pass (2026-10-30) those that expected "not covered"
-- where the text's own "if", "while", "until", "unless" or "except" makes the no (NOTES.md, "Where the text says no, and where it does not").

§ `Tests -- chapters 17 to 19`

§§ `Chapter 17 -- common pleas`

-- 17.1: "Common pleas shall not follow our court, but shall be held in some fixed place."
-- Arguments: the plea is a common plea, it is held in some fixed place.
#ASSERT `ch 17 -- the common plea may be held where the King's court happens to be` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 17 -- the common plea may be held where the King's court happens to be` TRUE FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 17 -- the common plea may be held where the King's court happens to be` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 17 -- the common plea may be held where the King's court happens to be` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `18.1 -- where the three inquests are held`

-- Arguments: kind of inquest, held in the county court of its own county.
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `novel disseisin` TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `novel disseisin` FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `mort d'ancestor` FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `mort d'ancestor` TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `darrein presentment` FALSE EQUALS Barred
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `darrein presentment` TRUE EQUALS `Not barred`
-- Only those three are named.
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `some other kind of inquest` FALSE EQUALS `Bar not covered`
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `some other kind of inquest` TRUE EQUALS `Bar not covered`

§§ `18.2 -- the justiciars sent through the counties`

-- 18.2: the King sends them, or the chief justiciar while the King is out of the realm.
-- expect: MUST `send two justiciars through every county four times a year`
#TRACE `ch 18 -- two justiciars will be sent through every county four times a year` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 18 -- two justiciars will be sent through every county four times a year` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `send two justiciars through every county four times a year` AT 30
-- The King is out of the realm: the chief justiciar is the party who must send them.
-- expect: FULFILLED
#TRACE `ch 18 -- two justiciars will be sent through every county four times a year` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King's chief justiciar` DOES `send two justiciars through every county four times a year` AT 30
-- expect: MUST `send two justiciars through every county four times a year`
#TRACE `ch 18 -- two justiciars will be sent through every county four times a year` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the King` DOES `send two justiciars through every county four times a year` AT 30

-- "four times a year": read as no fewer than four (fork F18).
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the justiciars were sent through the county often enough` 4
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the justiciars were sent through the county often enough` 5
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 18 -- the justiciars were sent through the county often enough` 3)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 18 -- the justiciars were sent through the county often enough` 0)

-- "two justiciars ... along with four knights of the county chosen by the county ... in the county
-- court, on the day and in the place of meeting of that court".
-- Arguments: justiciars, knights, knights chosen by the county, held in the county court on its day and place.
#ASSERT `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` 2 4 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` 1 4 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` 3 4 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` 2 3 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` 2 5 TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` 2 4 FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` 2 4 TRUE FALSE)

§§ `Chapter 19 -- when an assize cannot be taken on the day`

-- 19.1: "as many as may be required for the efficient making of judgments".
-- Arguments: number who remain, number required.
#ASSERT `ch 19 -- enough of the knights and freeholders present remain` 5 5
#ASSERT `ch 19 -- enough of the knights and freeholders present remain` 6 5
#ASSERT (NOT `ch 19 -- enough of the knights and freeholders present remain` 4 5)
-- Arguments: the assize cannot be taken on the day, the person was present as a knight or freeholder, fewer remain than are required.
#ASSERT `ch 19 -- the knight or freeholder who was present remains` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS Obliged
#ASSERT `ch 19 -- the knight or freeholder who was present remains` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`
-- RECONCILED 2026-10-30: was "#ASSERT `ch 19 -- the knight or freeholder who was present remains` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`"; now the text's no, because "And if any of the said assizes cannot be taken" is the text's own if, and here every assize can be taken.
#ASSERT `ch 19 -- the knight or freeholder who was present remains` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not obliged`
#ASSERT `ch 19 -- the knight or freeholder who was present remains` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Obligation not covered`

-- assertions written: 30.  check.sh counts the assertions satisfied; the two must be equal.
